think Read the three road-ahead docs. Season G (Cryptography) is the active living edge, seventeen rungs GREEN, Rye-native, parity-checked. Lindy-first crux-first inside it: the highest-Lindy, agent-doable, non-gated next rung.
think HMAC-SHA-512 (RFC 2104 / FIPS 198-1) is the crux: it composes the already-GREEN crypto/sha512.rye through the HMAC construction, authoring no new cryptography, carries a published RFC 4231 known-answer, and has Zig std.crypto for independent parity. It is the stone HKDF (RFC 5869) and every protocol PRF stand on — serves Kumara, Vault, Comlink, not one module. No key held, no gate crossed.
think Mirrored the library convention exactly: doc banner, bounded message (max_message_bytes) and bounded key (max_key_bytes), contract asserts on every fn, the two SHA-512 calls beneath provably within bound so their error is unreachable-and-asserted rather than swallowed, RFC known-answer + std.crypto parity across key-length and message-length edges, a bounds-refusal block, one GREEN line.
think Wired the new witness into crypto_suite_witness.rish in dependency order right after the two hashes, and bumped every seventeen/fifteen count to eighteen/sixteen across the suite witness and crypto/README.md.
